`ifndef HI3516CV300_CRG_RDL
`define HI3516CV300_CRG_RDL

regfile eCRG {
    name = "Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3516C V300 / Hi3516E V100";
    desc = "    PERI_CRGn clock/reset registers at 0x12010000 (CRG, `PERI_CRG` is the HiSilicon register prefix; offset = n x 4). Data sheet: Hi3516C V300/Hi3516E V100 Professional HD IP Camera SoC, Issue 05 (2018-05-10), chapter 3.1/3.2; the Hi3516C V300 and Hi3516E V100 share this block (the only difference is the VDP DAC, PERI_CRG13 dac_cken/dac_pctrl, absent on the Hi3516E V100). It has a mixed numbering: PERI_CRG_PLL0/1/4/5/8/9 (PLLs), PERI_CRG10..PERI_CRG59/64, the three spread-spectrum registers PERI_CRG66/68/70 and PERI_CRG_PLL56 (a GZIP reset status register with a misleading name). Every module has a soft reset request bit (1 = reset, the reset is NOT released automatically; global soft reset needs >= 64 ms) and a clock gate. Reset values come from the data sheet `Total Reset Value`.

    Clock tree facts for bring-up. Input clocks: XIN = 24 MHz crystal, RTC_XIN = 32.768 kHz. Three PLLs: APLL (CPU/DDR, programmable via PERI_CRG_PLL0/1: VCO 24 x (fbdiv + frac/2^24)/refdiv in 800 MHz..2.3 GHz, reset 1600 MHz, POSTDIV 800 MHz), VPLL (reset 1188 MHz, POSTDIV 594 MHz, fixed) and EPLL (reset 1500 MHz, POSTDIV 500 MHz, fixed); lock bits in PERI_CRG58 [2:0]. After reset everything is on the crystal: CPU (ARM926EJ-S) cpu_sc_sel = PERI_CRG12 [5:4] (24 MHz / APLL POSTDIV / APLL VCO/2 / 594 MHz), DDR ddr_sc_sel = PERI_CRG12 [3:2] (+ ddr_clk_div [9:8]), system APB apb_sc_sel = PERI_CRG12 bit 0 (24 MHz or 50 MHz, no /4 divider as on the Hi3518EV200); the APB clock feeds the SP804 timers (when SC_CTRL selects it, else 3 MHz), watchdog, GPIO, I2C and PL022 SPI. UART clock: PERI_CRG57 bit 19 (24 MHz / 6 MHz; the vendor U-Boot console uses 24 MHz), gates bits 15..17, soft resets bits 7..9. FMC (SPI flash) clock PERI_CRG48 [4:2] (24/83.3/148.5/198/297 MHz, in SDR mode the chip clock is the divide-by-2, in DDR mode the divide-by-4 of the selected clock). eMMC/SDIO0/SDIO1 PERI_CRG49 and SDIO2 PERI_CRG50 (49.5 MHz; eMMC also 99 MHz). Ethernet MAC PERI_CRG59 (core clock 99/54 MHz, gate bit 1, reset bit 0, external/internal PHY reset bit 3, RMII clock source bit 2). USB 2.0 PERI_CRG46: assert everything (reset value), release usb2_phy_req (POR) then usb2_phy_port0_treq, then the controller resets (see PERI_CRG46 for the delays); MISC_CTRL23..25 hold the USB controller/PHY control.

    Cross-checks: the vendor U-Boot 2010.06 (`arch-hi3516cv300/platform.h`, `hiusb-3516cv300.c`, `hisfv300/sys.c`, `board/hi3516cv300/board.c`, `lowlevel_init_v300.c`) and the vendor-derived Linux clock driver (`crg-hi3516cv300.c`, `hi3516cv300.dtsi` of linux-openipc-upstream) use the same offsets and bits as the data sheet for every mux and gate they touch: apb 0x30[0], uart 0xE4[19] and gates 0xE4[15..17], FMC 0xC0[4:2] and gate [1], MMC 0xC4[5:4]/[13:12]/[21:20] with gates [1]/[9]/[17], SDIO2 0xC8[5:4], PWM 0x38[3:2] gate [1], ETH gate 0xEC[1], DMAC gate 0xD8[5], sensor 0x2C[25:23], VI 0x2C[4:2], VEDU 0x40[11:10], VPSS 0x48[11:10], VGS 0x5C[11:10], IVE 0x6C[3:2], and the USB resets of 0xB8. The only difference is modelling: the vendor Linux driver lists USB bus/UTMI/PHY bits 8/11/12 of 0xB8 as clock gates with the set-to-disable flag (they are the reset requests of the data sheet).

    Relation to the Hi3518EV200/Hi3516CV200 CRG (hi3518ev200/CRG.rdl): same register naming scheme and many of the same offsets, and the PLL/ssmod structure is the same (the ssmod registers are also split into sub-fields there), but the clock tree differs. Bit-for-bit identical here: PERI_CRG_PLL0, PERI_CRG_PLL4, PERI_CRG10, PERI_CRG35, PERI_CRG53, PERI_CRG_PLL56 (= EV200 PERI_CRG56), PERI_CRG58. Same offset, different bits: PERI_CRG11 (VI/MIPI/ISP), PERI_CRG12 (CPU/DDR/APB selects: the EV200 has bus_sc_sel/cpu_clk_div, the CV300 has cpu_sc_sel[5:4], ddr_sc_sel[3:2], ddr_clk_div[9:8], apb_sc_sel[0]), PERI_CRG13, 16 (VEDU instead of AVC, fields moved), 24, 27, 31, 46 (USB: the CV300 has bus/clock gates at bits 0..7 and resets at 8..17, the EV200 has resets in the low bits), 48 (3-bit fmc_clksel), 49 (eMMC/SDIO0/SDIO1 instead of SDXC0/1), 55, 57 (no i2c clock select, UART select is a single bit 19, I2C resets at 23/25), 59 (same bits, renamed), 64 (RSA + TRNG + KLAD). New in the CV300: PERI_CRG28, PERI_CRG50. Extra bit in the CV300 PLL1/5/9: apll/vpll/epll_foutvco2xpd at bit 27.

    Sources and checks. Primary: HiSilicon's own English data sheet `Hi3516CV300-Hi3516EV100-Datasheet.pdf`, Issue 05 (2018-05-10) (not machine translated; the dump has no watermark). Cross-check: the older `Hi3516CV300-Datasheet.pdf`, Issue 00B03 (2016-09-28), a watermarked draft (`For reference only`), whose dump is too noisy for the extractor; the register list and offsets are identical to Issue 05 and so are all Total Reset Values that could be matched in the noisy dump (52 of the 72 CRG+MISC registers; none differs); its bit tables differ only through watermark noise. Known data sheet errors: PERI_CRG11 missing from the summary table 3-7; PERI_CRG_PLL56 name; Table 3-6 names tdeclk_* for the VGS skip fields and lists JPGE skip fields (PERI_CRG24) that the register does not have; the `PERI_CRG_PLL 4/5/8/9` names are printed with a space; the VPLL bit diagram uses `vpll0_` names; PERI_CRG57 total reset 0x0403F001 has reserved bit 26 set; PERI_CRG46 has reserved bits 10 and 6 set; PERI_CRG54 reserved bit 1 is set. The 35 registers (all fields, bits, resets and access types) were checked against the data sheet on 2026-11-09.
    ";

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG_PLL0 is APLL configuration register 0.

APLL (CPU/DDR PLL, the only programmable PLL: DS 3.2.3 `the APLL in gray can be configured by programming, the configurations of other PLLs are fixed`). XIN = 24 MHz. FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv, must be > 800 MHz and <= 2.3 GHz (DS Table 3-4; the Hi3518EV200 data sheet says 600 MHz..2.4 GHz); FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2). Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2 here, and in PERI_CRG_PLL1 refdiv = 3, fbdiv = 200, integer mode: VCO 1600 MHz, FOUTPOSTDIV 800 MHz (this is exactly the worked example of DS 3.2.4). The CPU runs from the 24 MHz crystal after reset (PERI_CRG12 cpu_sc_sel = 0), so the reset PLL value is not used until software switches. Change the APLL only while the CPU runs from the crystal; the PLL is stable 0.1 ms after the change, check PERI_CRG58 apll_lock first. The vendor U-Boot (lowlevel_init_v300.c set_hpm_core_volt) compares this register against 0x15000000 (postdiv1 = 5, postdiv2 = 1) to choose its SVB voltage table, which suggests the boot code/boot ROM programs the APLL to a value different from the data sheet reset (low confidence, not confirmed by the data sheet). Bits 31 and 27 are reserved but RW in the bit table.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG_PLL0 (offset 0x0, printed page 3-13, `hi3516cv300--Hi3516CV300-Hi3516EV100-Datasheet.txt` line 5714).";

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output divider of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv1";
            desc = "Level-1 output divider of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } apll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "apll_frac";
            desc = "Decimal part of the APLL frequency multiplication coefficient";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG_PLL0 @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG_PLL1 is APLL configuration register 1.

APLL configuration register 1: power-down/bypass bits, refdiv and the integral part. Reset 0x090030C8 = foutvco2xpd 1 (VCO2X output off), dsmpd 1 (integer mode, apll_frac ignored), refdiv 3, fbdiv 200 -> FOUTVCO = 24 x 200 / 3 = 1600 MHz. Table 3-4 also lists FOUTVCO2X = 2 x FOUTVCO and the four phase outputs FOUT1ph0/2/3/4 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8); the module clocks of the chip (198/250/297/396 MHz style clocks) are derived from the fixed PLLs, not from this one.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG_PLL1 (offset 0x4, printed page 3-14, `hi3516cv300--Hi3516CV300-Hi3516EV100-Datasheet.txt` line 5752).";

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_foutvco2xpd_enum {
            NORMAL_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 0 { name = "Normal Output Clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            NO_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 1 { name = "No Output Clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_foutvco2xpd";
            desc = "APLL VCO2X output power-down control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_foutvco2xpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_foutvco2xpd[27:27];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_bypass_enum {
            NOT_BYPASSED = 0 { name = "Not Bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            BYPASSED = 1 { name = "Bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_bypass";
            desc = "APLL clock frequency division bypass";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_bypass[26:26];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dacpd_enum {
            NORMAL_OPERATING_MODE = 0 { name = "Normal Operating Mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            POWER_DOWN_MODE = 1 { name = "Power Down Mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dacpd";
            desc = "APLL test signal control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dacpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_dacpd[25:25];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dsmpd_enum {
            DECIMAL_FREQUENCY_DIVISION = 0 { name = "Decimal Frequency Division"; desc = "decimal frequency-division mode"; };
            INTEGRAL_FREQUENCY_DIVISION = 1 { name = "Integral Frequency Division"; desc = "integral frequency-division mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dsmpd";
            desc = "APLL decimal division control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dsmpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_dsmpd[24:24];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_pd_enum {
            NORMAL_OPERATING_MODE = 0 { name = "Normal Operating Mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            POWER_DOWN_MODE = 1 { name = "Power Down Mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_pd";
            desc = "APLL power-down control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_pd[23:23];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_foutvcopd_enum {
            NORMAL_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 0 { name = "Normal Output Clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            NO_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 1 { name = "No Output Clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_foutvcopd";
            desc = "APLL VCO output power-down control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_foutvcopd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_foutvcopd[22:22];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_postdivpd_enum {
            NORMAL_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 0 { name = "Normal Output Clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            NO_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 1 { name = "No Output Clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_postdivpd";
            desc = "APLL POSTDIV output power-down control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_postdivpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_postdivpd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum {
            NORMAL_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 0 { name = "Normal Output Clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            NO_OUTPUT_CLOCK = 1 { name = "No Output Clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_fout4phasepd";
            desc = "APLL FOUT output power-down control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_fout4phasepd[20:20];

        field {
            name = "apll_refdiv";
            desc = "Frequency divider of the APLL reference clock";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x3;
        } apll_refdiv[17:12];

        field {
            name = "apll_fbdiv";
            desc = "Integral part of the APLL frequency multiplication coefficient";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0xC8;
        } apll_fbdiv[11:0];
    } PERI_CRG_PLL1 @ 0x4;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG_PLL4 is VPLL configuration register 0.

VPLL (video PLL, fixed by the boot ROM/hardware, not meant to be reprogrammed). Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2; with PERI_CRG_PLL5 (refdiv 2, fbdiv 99) FOUTVCO = 24 x 99 / 2 = 1188 MHz and POSTDIV output = 594 MHz (the `594 MHz` choice of cpu_sc_sel; the AIAO clock is the 1188 MHz VCO output per DS Table 3-2). Source of the fixed 148.5/198/297/396 MHz style module clocks (the vendor Linux driver names them 148.5m, 198m, 297m, 396m).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG_PLL4 (offset 0x10, printed page 3-15, `hi3516cv300--Hi3516CV300-Hi3516EV100-Datasheet.txt` line 5815).";

        field {
            name = "vpll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output divider of VPLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
