    reg {
        name = "Soft reset control register for other CRG interface modules";
        desc = "PERI_CRG57 is a soft reset control register for other CRG interface modules.

Soft resets and clock gates of the low-speed APB peripherals. Reset 0x0403F001: reserved bit 26 is set (modelled as the RO field reserved_nz_27_26), bits 17:12 (UART2/1/0, SSP1/0, IR clock gates) and test_clk_en are 1. UART clock: uart_clksel (bit 19) = 0 selects 24 MHz, 1 selects 6 MHz; there is only this one select for all three UARTs and no I2C clock select (the I2C controllers run from the APB clock, DT clocks = HI3516CV300_APB_CLK). The vendor U-Boot board.c sys_clk_rest_init() clears the console UART soft reset, enables its clock gate and sets uart_clksel to 24 MHz (CONFIG_PL011_CLOCK = 24 MHz), and the vendor Linux driver (uart_mux {24m, 6m} at 0xE4 bit 19, UART gates 15/16/17, SPI gates 13/14) agrees. The data sheet gives the I2C0 reset at bit 23 and the I2C1 reset at bit 25 (not contiguous).

